xnu 0280: an unattended drag, in the direction the UI actually pages

`mondriandrag=N` swept a synthetic finger vertically near the bottom edge for
three seconds of every N. On a home screen that gestures at the app switcher,
and a page that never moves draws nothing, so the sweep measured the frames of
a finished animation. Its motion also started at the first tick after boot,
before the UI is up.

The sweep is now horizontal along the middle of the panel, a round trip in two
seconds, and two boot arguments place it: `mondriandragsweep=S` seconds of
motion (default 3) and `mondriandragdelay=D` seconds before the first (default
0). `mondriandrag=100 mondriandragsweep=60 mondriandragdelay=40` gives three
60 s drags with idle gaps between them, in one boot, with nobody at the phone.

