 /*
- * Boot-arg mondriandrag=N: a synthetic finger that swipes up from the bottom
- * edge at the panel rate for three seconds every N seconds. The frame rate
- * then says whether the UI follows a 60 Hz stream of positions or whether
- * something else caps it, with no hand on the glass.
+ * Boot-arg mondriandrag=N: a synthetic finger that drags across the middle of
+ * the panel for mondriandragsweep seconds every N seconds, starting
+ * mondriandragdelay seconds in. A drag is the gesture that shows a stutter, so
+ * a phone left alone can still produce the measurement, and the delay lets the
+ * boot finish and the UI come up before the first sweep.
+ *
+ * The swipe is horizontal: that is the gesture that pages the home screen. A
+ * vertical one at the bottom edge opens the app switcher instead, and an
+ * animation that has finished drawing says nothing about the cadence.
